FFmpeg

The macOS app includes FFmpeg 8.1.3 (https://ffmpeg.org) as the separate
programs ffmpeg and ffprobe in Contents/MacOS. FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later. Its license text is in the
app at Contents/Resources/licenses/FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt and in this repository
at backend/licenses/FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt. scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh builds it
from the unmodified FFmpeg 8.1.3 release with LGPL components only, without
--enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree or --enable-version3. The FFmpeg 8.1.3 source
code is available from ffmpeg.org at
https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.3.tar.xz.

AI voiceover

The app runs ONNX Runtime (https://onnxruntime.ai), Copyright (c) Microsoft
Corporation, under the MIT License, through the ort crate (MIT or Apache 2.0).
It phonemizes English with misaki-rs (https://github.com/MicheleYin/misaki-rs),
Copyright (c) 2026 Michele Yin, under the MIT License, which includes the
dictionaries of misaki (https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki) under the Apache
License 2.0. On first use the app downloads the Kokoro-82M voice model and
voices (https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX), licensed
under the Apache License 2.0; they are not part of the app. espeak-ng is not
used.
